From: Redmi 7 onclite kernel build
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: configs: onclite: allow unsigned modules

Keep module signature verification enabled, but do not require every module
loaded by the Redmi 7 kernel to have a trusted signature. The module loader
continues to reject invalid signatures and all other module checks remain in
place.

---
 arch/arm64/configs/onclite-perf_defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/onclite-perf_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/onclite-perf_defconfig
index 04ecaf84f9369f930f3aadad0f4c218255070432..38146b063fa80490084a9d720527a78dddd3d50e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/onclite-perf_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/onclite-perf_defconfig
@@ -50,6 +50,6 @@ CONFIG_MODULE_FORCE_UNLOAD=y
 CONFIG_MODVERSIONS=y
 CONFIG_MODULE_SIG=y
-CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_FORCE=y
+# CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_FORCE is not set
 CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_SHA512=y
 # CONFIG_BLK_DEV_BSG is not set
 CONFIG_PARTITION_ADVANCED=y
